<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;KUNSTGEWERBEMUSEUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kunstgewerbemuseum was founded in 1874 and later became the Museum of Applied Arts, known for its historical exhibits and renovations."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEW GRASSI BUILDING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The New Grassi Building is the current location of the Museum of Applied Arts, housing numerous exhibits since 1926."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WORLD WAR II&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"World War II caused significant damage to the Museum of Applied Arts, including the destruction of many exhibits."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRASSI MUSEUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grassi Museum refers to the Museum of Applied Arts before it received its present name in 2005."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLUE BOOK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blue Book is a document listing 'Cultural Lighthouses' recognized by the German government, with the Museum of Applied Arts included."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSEUM OF APPLIED ARTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Museum of Applied Arts is a renowned museum in Budapest, known for its extensive collections and architectural significance."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BUDAPEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Budapest is the city where the Museum of Applied Arts is located, known for its rich cultural heritage and Art Nouveau architecture."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ÖDÖN LECHNER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ödön Lechner is the architect of the Museum of Applied Arts, known for designing the building in the Art Nouveau style."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOPP FERENC MUSEUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hopp Ferenc Museum is another location associated with the Museum of Applied Arts, though separate from the main building."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ÜLLŐI ÚT 33-37&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Üllői út 33-37 is the specific address of the main Museum building in Budapest."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMERICAN MUSEUM OF CERAMIC ART&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"American Museum of Ceramic Art is a separate museum located in Los Angeles, focusing on ceramic art collections."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ART NOUVEAU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Art Nouveau is the architectural and design style used in the construction of the Museum of Applied Arts, characterized by flowing lines and organic forms."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GYULA PÁRTOS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gyula Pártos is mentioned as a co-designer of the Museum of Applied Arts along with Ödön Lechner, contributing to its Art Nouveau design."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREEN ROOF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Green Roof is a feature of the Museum of Applied Arts, designed to blend with the natural environment and enhance the building's aesthetic appeal."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLLECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Collection includes metalwork, furniture, textiles, and glass, representing various aspects of applied arts."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIBRARY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Library is part of the Museum of Applied Arts, containing resources related to the museum's collections and exhibitions."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOS ANGELES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Los Angeles is the city where the American Museum of Ceramic Art is located."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GEORGES DE FEURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Georges de Feure is mentioned as the designer of a floor vase displayed at the Museum of Applied Arts."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAKAB RAPOPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jakab Rapoport is mentioned as the craftsman who executed a floor vase designed by Georges de Feure."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLOOR VASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Floor Vase is a specific exhibit at the Museum of Applied Arts, designed by Georges de Feure and executed by Jakab Rapoport."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GYÖRGY RÁTH VILLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"György Ráth Villa is another notable building associated with the Museum of Applied Arts, though separate from the main museum."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RENOVATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Renovation is a planned project for the Museum of Applied Arts, aimed at restoring and improving the building."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CULTURAL LIGHTHOUSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cultural Lighthouses are recognized institutions listed in the German government's Blue Book, with the Museum of Applied Arts included."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUNGARY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hungary is the country where the Museum of Applied Arts is located, known for its rich cultural heritage."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMM.HU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"WEBSITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"imm.hu is the website of the Museum of Applied Arts, providing information about the museum and its collections."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1091 BUDAPEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1091 Budapest is the postal code of the main Museum building in Budapest."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIEW OF THE MAIN MUSEUM BUILDING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"IMAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"View of the main Museum building is a specific image showcasing the exterior of the museum designed by Ödön Lechner and Gyula Pártos."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GEORGIAN DESIGN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Georgian Design is mentioned as a style used in the floor vase designed by Georges de Feure and executed by Jakab Rapoport."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Paris is mentioned as the city where the floor vase was executed by Jakab Rapoport."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERAMIC ART&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ceramic Art is the focus of the American Museum of Ceramic Art, located in Los Angeles."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METALWORK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metalwork is part of the collection at the Museum of Applied Arts, showcasing various metal artifacts."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FURNITURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Furniture is part of the collection at the Museum of Applied Arts, showcasing various pieces of furniture."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEXTILES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Textiles is part of the collection at the Museum of Applied Arts, showcasing various textile items."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glass is part of the collection at the Museum of Applied Arts, showcasing various glass artifacts."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0171-cd88d9fb829c</data>
    </node>
